/**
 * Wisconsin Salesperson Pre-License (72 clock hours) — module question bank.
 *
 * REEB 25.033 fixes the course at 72 hours and lists nineteen topics that "shall" be included. It
 * allocates NO hours among them, prescribes no assessment, and sets no passing score. So the module
 * grouping, the hour allocation and the 80 percent engagement threshold are all StateCourse decisions
 * for Board review, and every document must say so — the opposite of Maine, where the Commission sets
 * both the weights and the passing grade.
 *
 * These items are NOT a licensing examination. They gate progression through a module and are visible
 * to the student by design.
 *
 * Each of the thirteen modules carries one applied item, five engagement items and five remediation
 * items. The correct answer is authored at index 0 for legibility and is permuted deterministically per
 * item id at delivery, so a recorded selection keeps its meaning permanently.
 *
 * Every Wisconsin section cited was read directly from docs.legis.wisconsin.gov on 2026-08-20 and is
 * recorded in wisconsin/regulatory/primary-text-readings.md. Where a source has NOT been read — ch.
 * REEB 15 through 24, ch. 706, ch. 709, ch. 766, ch. 779, ch. 236, ATCP 93 and 134, s. 106.50, and the
 * environmental chapters — no item asks a student to recall a figure from it. The authored answer is
 * the routing.
 *
 * Source correction 2026-09-06 supersedes that historical unread-source limitation for REEB 15,
 * 16, 17, 18, 23, 24, ATCP 134.07/.09 and the specified 106.50 provisions. See the dated review.
 *
 * Course version 1.0 submission draft — not approved. No Wisconsin pre-license credit is available.
 */

